@startuml 02-model
' The model at the abstraction level of the architecture document: the aggregate, the
' phases it moves through, and what a ship is made of. Field-by-field detail belongs in
' docs/uml/detailed, which is generated from the source.
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
title Galaxy Trucker — the model

class Game <<aggregate root>> {
  +apply(player, command) : Reaction
  +tick() : List<Event>
  +viewFor(player) : GameView
  +history() : List<Recorded>
  +restore(snapshot, ...) : Game
}

interface Phase {
  +apply(player, command) : Reaction
  +next() : Optional<Phase>
  +pending() : Optional<PlayerPrompt>
}

class BuildingPhase
class ValidationPhase
class CrewPhase
class FlightPhase
class ScoringPhase
class FinishedPhase

Phase <|.. BuildingPhase
Phase <|.. ValidationPhase
Phase <|.. CrewPhase
Phase <|.. FlightPhase
Phase <|.. ScoringPhase
Phase <|.. FinishedPhase

class Ship {
  +weld(cell)
  +discard(cell)
  +correct(cell)
  +attributes(plan) : ShipAttributes
  +pieces() : List<Set<Position>>
}

class ShipGrid
class ShipValidator
class Flight {
  +route()
  +giveUp(player)
  +stillFlying()
}
class AdventureDeck
class ComponentPool

interface AdventureCard {
  +resolve(flight) : AdventureResolution
}

class AdventureResolution {
  +pending() : Optional<PlayerPrompt>
  +submit(choice)
}

Game "1" *-- "1" Phase : is in
Game "1" *-- "2..4" Ship
Game "1" *-- "0..1" Flight
Game "1" *-- "1" AdventureDeck
Game "1" *-- "1" ComponentPool
Ship *-- ShipGrid
Ship ..> ShipValidator : checked by
FlightPhase --> AdventureCard : turns over
AdventureCard --> AdventureResolution : produces
FlightPhase --> AdventureResolution : asks and answers

note bottom of Game
  One thread per game. The model has no
  synchronisation of its own because it is
  never touched by two.
end note

note right of AdventureResolution
  Every card is a sequence of questions
  and the answers to them. That is why
  the flight is two commands rather than
  one per card type.
end note
@enduml
